# Local PROXY_IP rules (highest priority, one per line, '#' starts a comment).
#
# These are the ranges the Surge configuration already handles in its own PROXY_IP
# rule set, so the workflow keeps them out of the generated proxy-ip.list: the two
# layers stay complementary instead of repeating each other. Ranges published
# upstream that are not covered here still show up in the generated file.

# Apple's officially published core ranges
# (IPv4 plus three IPv6 ranges, see support.apple.com/en-us/103229)
IP-CIDR,17.0.0.0/8
IP-CIDR6,2403:300::/32
IP-CIDR6,2620:149::/32
IP-CIDR6,2a01:b740::/32

